          {
            ":db/id": 17592186125335,
            ":step/content": {
              ":db/id": 17592186125758,
              ":tutorial/content": "To find the pivots and pivot columns of a general matrix, we first need to convert the matrix to row echelon form (REF).\n\n- The pivots of any matrix are the pivots of its row equivalent REF matrix.\n\n- The pivot columns of a matrix are the pivot columns of its row equivalent REF matrix.\n\nTo reduce a general $n\\times m$ matrix to row echelon form, we follow a similar procedure to the $2\\times 2$ and $3\\times 3$ cases, as we'll see in the next example.",
              ":tutorial/id": "d45a4eba-96ce-5bef-92b7-b8f0d4cd8b72",
              ":tutorial/math-academy-id": 3158,
              ":tutorial/title": "Pivot Columns of a General Matrix"
            },
