                ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4706",
                ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n",
                ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+\\left(-\\frac{2}{7}\\right){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."
